                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I’ve played this game on 1991 when i got my first computer. I played it all my living hours as possible (i was 15 and shared the computer with my big family). \n\nMy original computer was an XT clone with Hercules Amber monitor. No mouse. No harddrive. No Soundcard. \n\nThe game came in two floppy disks 5 1/4”. \n\nI had the photocopies of the door codes, barely legible. \n\nI bought my copy on the local computer store 2 blocks from my dad’s home. \n\nThere was no legal software in Argentina or any way to get this software legally. \n\nDiscovered almost 4 endings all by myself. When I blew up the hamster i realized this game had a depth that was beyond my wildest dreams. \n\nMany years later I couldn’t believe that Ron Gilbert said with Jeff there was a possible ending. \n\nLuckily I’ve found that way too. \n\nI’ve been living like a brain donor for almost 30 years. \n\nFor another 30 years now that I’m a legal owner of this game thank to the magic of steam!! \n\n",
